These files are taken verbatim from qtbase, revision
db406557ae5ac393bd700f552214d950a4801bd8 (the SRCREV meta-qt6 builds for
6.12), from

    src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/

Qt 6.10 moved the QtWayland client into qtbase and, in doing so, stopped
publishing the client-side EGL hardware integration as the private module
QtWaylandEglClientHwIntegration; qtbase now builds the same sources as a
plugin only (QWaylandEglClientBufferPlugin), installing no headers and
exporting no symbols.

webos-wayland-egl subclasses QWaylandEglWindow and
QWaylandEglClientBufferIntegration, so it needs the types, not the plugin.
Rather than patch qtbase - which meta-qt6 would have to carry across every
upgrade - the sources are compiled directly into the webos plugin.

They keep their original Qt licence (LGPL-3.0-only or GPL-2.0-only, per the
headers); see the SPDX tags in each file. Refresh them from the same path when
the qtbase SRCREV moves.
